## Configure

Set `{{ destination_env }}` to the directory the copies are kept in:

```console
$ export {{ destination_env }}=/mnt/backup/{{ name }}
```

## The protocol

A transport is an ordinary executable. {{ host }} runs it twice:

```console
$ {{ bin_name }} --manifest   # what it does, as JSON on stdout
$ {{ bin_name }} run          # a request as JSON on stdin, a report on stdout
```

The manifest declares the protocol version, a name, and the operations this
transport offers:

```jsonc
{
  "protocol_version": {{ protocol_version }},
  "name": "{{ name }}",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "operations": [{{ operation_list }}]
}
```

A request arrives as `{"operation": "push", "file": "…", "name": "…"}`: {{ request_about }}.
The report may carry `message` (shown to the person) or `error`; printing
nothing is success with nothing to say.

Transports live for the duration of one call. Nothing here starts a service.

